Sql.CDATA:
DECLARE @ZPL INT = 26; DECLARE @PNG INT = 16; DECLARE @PDF INT = 6; DECLARE @LABELARY UNIQUEIDENTIFIER = 'F0E86E77-5279-4A1F-8626-1BCF760974DF'; DECLARE @PDFIMAGE UNIQUEIDENTIFIER = '28095542-A6FD-483C-8E47-A9748B4C622A'; DECLARE @LABELZOOM UNIQUEIDENTIFIER = '4138A60A-71F1-46DB-AF05-4678D42D5D54';
-- Insert 1: LABELARY (ZPL to PNG) INSERT INTO [dbo].[ALSetupRenderer] ( [CompanyID], RecordID, Active, [FromContent], [ToContent], [RenderingPrinterID], [NoteID], [CreatedByID], [CreatedByScreenID], [CreatedDateTime], [LastModifiedByID], [LastModifiedByScreenID], [LastModifiedDateTime] ) SELECT s.[CompanyID], @LABELARY, 1, @ZPL, @PNG, @LABELARY, NEWID(), s.[CreatedByID], s.[CreatedByScreenID], s.[CreatedDateTime], s.[LastModifiedByID], s.[LastModifiedByScreenID], s.[LastModifiedDateTime] FROM [dbo].[ALSetup] s WHERE NOT EXISTS ( SELECT 1 FROM [dbo].[ALSetupRenderer] sr WHERE sr.FromContent = @ZPL AND sr.ToContent = @PNG AND sr.RenderingPrinterID = @LABELARY );
-- Insert 2: PDFIMAGE (PDF to PNG) INSERT INTO [dbo].[ALSetupRenderer] ( [CompanyID], RecordID, Active, [FromContent], [ToContent], [RenderingPrinterID], [NoteID], [CreatedByID], [CreatedByScreenID], [CreatedDateTime], [LastModifiedByID], [LastModifiedByScreenID], [LastModifiedDateTime] ) SELECT s.[CompanyID], @PDFIMAGE, 1, @PDF, @PNG, @PDFIMAGE, NEWID(), s.[CreatedByID], s.[CreatedByScreenID], s.[CreatedDateTime], s.[LastModifiedByID], s.[LastModifiedByScreenID], s.[LastModifiedDateTime] FROM [dbo].[ALSetup] s WHERE NOT EXISTS ( SELECT 1 FROM [dbo].[ALSetupRenderer] sr WHERE sr.FromContent = @PDF AND sr.ToContent = @PNG AND sr.RenderingPrinterID = @PDFIMAGE );
-- Insert 3: LABELZOOM (ZPL to PNG, inactive) INSERT INTO [dbo].[ALSetupRenderer] ( [CompanyID], RecordID, Active, [FromContent], [ToContent], [RenderingPrinterID], [NoteID], [CreatedByID], [CreatedByScreenID], [CreatedDateTime], [LastModifiedByID], [LastModifiedByScreenID], [LastModifiedDateTime] ) SELECT s.[CompanyID], @LABELZOOM, 0, @ZPL, @PNG, @LABELZOOM, NEWID(), s.[CreatedByID], s.[CreatedByScreenID], s.[CreatedDateTime], s.[LastModifiedByID], s.[LastModifiedByScreenID], s.[LastModifiedDateTime] FROM [dbo].[ALSetup] s WHERE NOT EXISTS ( SELECT 1 FROM [dbo].[ALSetupRenderer] sr WHERE sr.FromContent = @ZPL AND sr.ToContent = @PNG AND sr.RenderingPrinterID = @LABELZOOM );

WikiRevision.column:
Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AL206500|AL206500])[anchor|#_da80ec49-7fcd-453f-9347-8fea2cd39f32]{br}
On this form, you can create, view, and edit model substitution. Substitutions are used in the expression tab of the [17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] ([~/?ScreenId=AL201000|AL201000]) form to allow you to format, calculate, extract the string from an expression. In other words, substitution allows you to manipulate a string or an array of strings that are pulled from your data in Acumatica or from the fixed/sample values that you enter. A use case for this would be to append the city, state, and zip code of a shipment address, or to format the weight of a product to round up to 2 decimal on the label. {br}
{TOC}
==Form Toolbar== [anchor|#_98898224-20bf-49fd-a9f1-0289e7377fe4] The form toolbar includes standard and form-specific buttons and commands. For the list of standard buttons, see [dfac4724-edbc-468e-9569-877c174ac871|Form Toolbar]. The form-specific commands (which can be shown as buttons on the form toolbar, as commands on the More menu, or in both places) are listed in the following table in alphabetical order. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Command !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Load Default Substitutions''' | Loads all the default substitutions which are functions from scriban, regex, Acumatica and our own defined functions. Each function will allow you to manipulate or modify the string expressions to which the substitution is assigned to. |}[anchor|#1] ==Summary Area== In this area, you can select an existing substitutions by its unique identifier or specify summary information about a new substitution. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Element !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Substitution ID''' | The unique identifier for the substitution. |- | '''Active'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the substitution is active in the system |- | '''Export''' | A check box that includes (if selected) the substitution to the export all file. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the substitution entered. |- | '''Is Composite''' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the substitution is a composite from another substitution. In other words, the substitution has different parameters or formats a string differently from the original setting. |- | '''System''' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the substitution is a default function from the system. System substitutions include functions that are from Acumatica, Scriban or ZPL functions. |- | '''Substitution Type''' | Describes the type of function the system substitution follows. It could be an Acumatica DateTime function, an Array function, a ZPL function, a math function, etc. |- | '''Function''' | The name of the function. |- | '''Signature''' | The signature describes the return type of the function. Some of the signatures could be boolean (bool), string, integer (int), object, double, etc. The return type of the variable is followed by the method and its parameters. |- | '''InternalName''' | The internal name of the function. |}[anchor|#2] ==Used By Models Tab== The '''Used by Models''' tab contains the list of label models that use the current substitution. The system automatically enters the models in the list as they are assigned the substitution from the [17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] form. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Model ID''' | The unique identifier that defines the label model in the system that uses the current substitution. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the label model selected. |- | '''Code''' | The name of the variable or expression that the substitution is tied to. |- | '''Active''' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the expression is active in the system. |- | '''Last Modified By''' | The user name of the person who last modified the label substitution. |- | '''Last Modified On''' | The date when the record was modified most recently. {br} |}[anchor|#11] ==Substitution Details Tab== The '''Substitution Detail''' tab contains the list of substitutions that make up the composite. This tab appears only if the ''Is Composite'' check box is enabled in the summary area of this form. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Active''' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the substitution is active in the system |- | '''Child Substitution''' | The unique identifier for the substitution that the composite is made from. |- | '''Subs. Arg. 1''' | The first argument /parameter passed in the function when the substitution is invoked. |- | '''Subs. Arg. 2''' | The second argument /parameter passed in the function when the substitution is invoked. |- | '''Subs. Arg. 3''' | The third argument /parameter passed in the function when the substitution is invoked. |- | '''Subs. Arg. 4''' | The fourth argument /parameter passed in the function when the substitution is invoked. |- | '''Subs. Arg. 5''' | The fifth argument /parameter passed in the function when the substitution is invoked. |- | '''Subs. Arg. 6''' | The sixth argument /parameter passed in the function when the substitution is invoked. |}[anchor|#11] ==Related Articles== *[17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] *[https://github.com/scriban/scriban/tree/master/doc|Scriban Documentation]

Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AL202000|AL202000]){br}
You use this form to view, configure, and create label dimensions and orientation. A label format describes the physical characteristics of a physical label and the printer configuration expected to print this label. Labels have different widths and heights and may be printed on printers having different printing densities (dots per inches or mm), qualities and orientations. For example, a classic example would be a 4 x 6 inches label with a density of 8 dots per mm (203 dots per in). In order to simplify those combinations, you can create as many formats as needed and re-use them across multiple label models. When the formats are created, the corresponding label format will be visible on the Format ID selector found in [17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] ([~/?ScreenId=AL201000|AL201000]) summary area. {TOC}
==Summary Area== In this area, you can view the list of label formats.
===Table Columns=== {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Active''' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the label format is active and available for selection on the forms. |- | '''Format ID''' | The unique identifier of the label format. |- | '''Description''' | The brief description provided for the label format. |- | '''Rotation''' | The orientation that the label will take when it is printed. The following options are available: *''0°'': 0 degree orientation; the label will be printed from bottom to top. *''90°'': 90 degrees orientation; the label will be flipped clockwise and be printed from right to left. *''180°'': 180 degrees orientation; the label will be flipped upside down and be printed from top to bottom. *''270°'': 270 degrees orientation; the label will be flipped counter clockwise and be printed from left to right. |- | '''Print Density''' | The measurement of light reflected off of the substrate, or how dark the print appears after each imprinted dot. It is expressed as dots per millimeter (dpmm) or dots per inch (dpi). The higher the density, the sharper the print quality. The print density you select will depend on the printer you are using. Make sure you look at the specifications of your printer to determine the correct print density to choose from. The following options are available: *''6 dpmm (152 dpi)'': Expressed as 6 dots per millimeter, for every millimeter on the label, 6 dots are printed. *''8 dpmm (203 dpi)'': Expressed as 8 dots per millimeter, for every millimeter on the label, 8 dots are printed. *''12 dpmm (304 dpi)'': Expressed as 12 dots per millimeter, for every millimeter on the label, 12 dots are printed. *''24 dpmm (609 dpi)'': Expressed as 24 dots per millimeter, for every millimeter on the label, 24 dots are printed. |- | '''Width''' | The width of the label in the unit of measure selected in the Size Unit. |- | '''Height''' | The height of the label in the unit of measure selected in the Size Unit. |- | '''Size Unit''' | The unit of measure dictating the dimension of the label. The following options are available: *''inch'': The unit of measure that corresponds to an inch. *''cm'': The unit of measure that corresponds to a centimeter. *''mm'': The unit of measure that corresponds to a millimeter. |- | '''Width (Dots)''' | The calculated width of the label in dots. |- | '''Height (Dots)''' | The calculated height of the label in dots. |- | '''Use With PDF''' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the format is to be used with a PDF. For instance, this could be used for larger formats which would be used for reports or packing slips. |}[anchor|#10] ==Used By Models Tab== The '''Used by Models''' tab contains the list of label models that use the current format. The system automatically displays the label models as they are assigned the specified format. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Model ID''' | The unique identifier that defines the label model in the system that uses the current label format. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the label model selected. |- | '''Last Modified By''' | The user name of the person who last modified the user, printer ID, or duplicate in toolbar checkbox. |- | '''Last Modified On''' | The date when the record was modified most recently. {br} |}[anchor|#11]
==Related Articles== *[17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] *[cc1f569a-e509-4277-86f0-713e588bab2e|Label Printers] *[1a5cba5d-64ad-4ff3-aad4-877ccdab962f|Label Preferences] ([~/?ScreenId=AL101000|AL101000]) *[https://www.porelon.com/improve-print-quality-print-density-foam/#:~:text=Print%20density%20is%20the%20measurement,role%20in%20print%20density%20quality.|Additional information on Print Density] *[https://bmiimaging.com/blog/document-management/bitonal-vs-grayscale/|Additional information on Print Quality]

Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AL501000|AL501000]){br}
On this form, you can select the print job, specify criteria for selecting label model to be considered for deletion, and delete all of the filtered print jobs or only selected ones.
==Form Toolbar==[anchor|#_5ee4beb4-e984-4400-b0b5-e6531fe75590] The form toolbar includes standard and form-specific buttons and commands. For the list of standard buttons, see [dfac4724-edbc-468e-9569-877c174ac871|Form Toolbar]. The form-specific commands are listed in the following table.[anchor|#table_rcj_4ms_2bb]
{| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Command !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Delete''' | Initiates the selected deletion (based on the '''Action''' you select) for the label print jobs you have selected (by using the select) in the table. |- | '''Delete All''' | Initiates the selected deletion (based on the '''Action''' you select) for all label print jobs listed in the table. |}[anchor|#1]
==Selection Area== In this area, you can define the criteria for the print job of label model to be displayed in the table, as well as the action to be applied if you click '''Delete''' or '''Delete All'''.[anchor|#table_g2j_4ms_2bb] {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Element !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Status''' | The processing status of the print job, which can be one of the following:[anchor|#ul_f2w_fzz_xcb] *''Processed'': The print job has been processed successfully. *''Pending'': The print job is waiting for processing. *''Failed'': The print job failed to process. *''Unknown'': Unknown processing of print jobs. |- | '''End Date''' | The end date of the date range for the label print jobs. You can leave the box blank to view all print jobs. |}[anchor|#2] ==Table== This table contains the list of print jobs of label model that match any criteria specified in the Selection area. You can select print jobs for processing by using the check boxes in the select column. [anchor|#table_vfj_4ms_2bb] {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Job ID''' | The identifier of a print job. |- | '''Description''' | The description of a print job. |- | '''DeviceHub ID''' | The unique identifier of the DeviceHub application in which the printer is configured. |- | '''Printer''' | The name of the printer to which the report was sent for printing. |- | '''Number of Copies''' | The number of copies of label models that were printed. |- | '''Status''' | The processing status of the print job, which can be one of the following:[anchor|#ul_f2w_fzz_xcb] *''Processed'': The print job has been processed successfully. *''Pending'': The print job is waiting for processing. *''Failed'': The print job failed to process. |- | '''Creation Date and Time''' | The date and time when the printing operation was run. |}

Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AL205000|AL205000])[anchor|#_da80ec49-7fcd-453f-9347-8fea2cd39f32]{br}
On this form, you can create, view, and edit model margins. Model margins dictate the white space present on the left, right, top and bottom of a label model. By setting model margins, the physical dimensions of editable text on the label are reduced. {br}{TOC}
==Summary Area== In this area, you can select an existing model margins by its unique identifier or specify summary information about a new margins. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Element !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Margin ID''' | The unique identifier of the model margins. |- | '''Active'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the model margin is active in the system |- | '''Export'' | A check box that includes (if selected) the margin to the export all file. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the margin entered. |- | '''Size Unit''' | The unit of measure dictating the dimension of the margins. |- | '''Left''' | Defines the space outside the element, on the left side. |- | '''Right'' | Defines the space outside the element, on the right side. |- | '''Top'' | Defines the space outside the element, on the top. |- | '''Bottom'' | Defines the space outside the element, on the bottom. |}[anchor|#2] ==Used By Models Tab== The '''Used By Models''' tab contains the list of label models that follows the current margin. The system automatically list the models as they are assigned to the margin from the [17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] form. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Model ID''' | The unique identifier that defines the label model in the system that uses the current model rule. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the label model selected. |- | '''Last Modified By''' | The user name of the person who last modified the user, printer ID, or duplicate in toolbar checkbox. |- | '''Last Modified On''' | The date when the record was modified most recently. |}[anchor|#11] ==Related Articles== *[17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models]

Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AL207000|AL207000])[anchor|#_da80ec49-7fcd-453f-9347-8fea2cd39f32]{br}
On this form, you can create, view, edit and load default fonts that are available for printing and placement on a label model. You can load the fonts that are registered on the Zebra ZPL programming guide at their default setting by clicking on the ''Load Default Fonts'' button on the toolbar. Fonts are editable from their default setting and given specific options regarding height, and width. There are different fonts to select from, each with their own set of proportions and appearance. There are two types of font: '''Monospaced '''and '''Proportional'''.
''Monospace ''is a font whose letters and characters each occupy the same amount of horizontal space. {br} ''Proportional ''is a font where each character occupies only as much width as it needs. {br} {TOC}
==Form Toolbar== [anchor|#_98898224-20bf-49fd-a9f1-0289e7377fe4] The form toolbar includes standard and form-specific buttons and commands. For the list of standard buttons, see [dfac4724-edbc-468e-9569-877c174ac871|Form Toolbar]. The form-specific commands (which can be shown as buttons on the form toolbar, as commands on the More menu, or in both places) are listed in the following table in alphabetical order. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Command !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Load Default Fonts''' | Loads all the fonts that are said to be available in the ZPL II programming guide, at their default setting. Said fonts are identified from values A through Z and 0 to 9. |- | '''Render''' | Renders the sample value inputted in the current font. |}[anchor|#1]
==Summary Area== In this area, you can select an existing barcode by its unique identifier or specify summary information about a modifications to default fonts. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Element !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Font ID''' | The unique identifier of the font. If barcodes are loaded from the toolbar button ''Load Default Fonts'', then the unique identifier are generated automatically by the system. The identifier follows the font code given from the ZPL II language command. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the type of font and its specific options (if applicable) for differentiation. |- | '''Font Type''' | The type of the Font |- | '''Height''' | The height of the text in the font style. |- | '''Width''' | The width of the text in the font style. |- | '''Active'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the font is active in the system |- | '''Export''' | A check box that includes (if selected) the font to the export all file. |- | '''Language''' | The printer control language of the defined font. |- | '''Sample Value''' | The value used in the rendering process of the font text. Sample values are independent of the values used for printing or placed on the label. |- | '''Render Message''' | The messages or warnings displayed in case of a rendering issue. |}[anchor|#2] ==Related Articles== *[17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] *[https://www.zebra.com/content/dam/zebra_new_ia/en-us/manuals/printers/common/programming/zpl-zbi2-pm-en.pdf|ZPL II, ZBI 2, Set-Get-Do, Mirror, WML Programming Guide] *[https://intercom.help/asgard-alliance-inc/en/collections/3586338-available-fonts|Fonts Help Center]

Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AL207500|AL207500])[anchor|#_da80ec49-7fcd-453f-9347-8fea2cd39f32]{br}
On this form, you can create, view, and edit categories. Categories allow you to create different filters for label models. {br}{TOC}
==Summary Area== In this area, you can select an existing categories by its unique identifier or specify summary information about a new category. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Element !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Category ID''' | The unique identifier of the category. |- | '''Active'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the category is active in the system |- | '''Export''' | A check box that includes (if selected) the category to the export all file. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the category entered. |}[anchor|#2] ==Used By Models Tab== The '''Used By Models''' tab contains the list of label models that follows the current category. The system automatically lists the models as they are assigned to the category from the [17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] form. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Model ID''' | The unique identifier that defines the label model in the system that uses the current category. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the label model selected. |- | '''Last Modified By''' | The user name of the person who last modified the category assignment of label. |- | '''Last Modified On''' | The date when the record was modified most recently. |}[anchor|#11] ==Related Articles== * [17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models]

Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AL208000|AL208000])[anchor|#_da80ec49-7fcd-453f-9347-8fea2cd39f32]{br}
On this form, you can create, view, and edit sequences. Sequences are used by contents [e3990d02-4890-48b3-8d01-511bad4776cd|Contents] ([~/?ScreenId=AL206000|AL206000]). Sequences are the encoders, ASCII decimals, functions that complex barcodes used to populate data such as GS1 barcodes. {br}
{TOC}
==Summary Area== In this area, you can select an existing sequence by its unique identifier or specify summary information about a new sequence. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Element !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Substitution ID''' | The unique identifier for the substitution. |- | '''Active'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the sequence is active in the system |- | '''Export''' | A check box that includes (if selected) the sequence to the export all file. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the sequence. |- | '''System''' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the sequence is a default function from the system. System sequences include functions that are ASCII unprintable characters, ZPL encoded strings and ZPL functions. |- | '''Sequence Type''' | Describes the type of function the system sequence follows. It could be a string or an ASCII decimal. |- | '''Content''' | The name of the content that uses the sequence. |}[anchor|#2]
==Used By Content Tab== The '''Used by Content''' tab contains the list of contents that use the current sequence. The system automatically enters the content in the list as they are assigned the sequence from the [e3990d02-4890-48b3-8d01-511bad4776cd|Contents] form. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Content ID''' | The unique identifier that defines the content in the system that uses the current sequence. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the content selected. |- | '''Last Modified By''' | The user name of the person who last modified the label sequence. |- | '''Last Modified On''' | The date when the record was modified most recently. {br} |}[anchor|#11]
==Related Articles== *[e3990d02-4890-48b3-8d01-511bad4776cd|Contents]

Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AL204500|AL204500])[anchor|#_da80ec49-7fcd-453f-9347-8fea2cd39f32]{br}
On this form, you can create, view, and edit print stations. Print Stations contain a list of Label Printers [cc1f569a-e509-4277-86f0-713e588bab2e|Label Printers] ([~/?ScreenId=AL203000|AL203000]). Print stations are a hub for multiple printers. {br}
{TOC}
==Summary Area== In this area, you can select an existing print station by its unique identifier or specify summary information about a new print station. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Element !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Print Station ID''' | The unique identifier for the print station. |- | '''Active'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the print station is active in the system |- | '''Export''' | A check box that includes (if selected) the print station to the export all file. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the print station. |}[anchor|#2]
==Used By Model Printers Tab== The '''Used by Model Printer''' tab contains the list of printers that are a part of the print station. The system automatically enters the printers in the list as they are assigned the print station from the [cc1f569a-e509-4277-86f0-713e588bab2e|Label Printers] form. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Model ID''' | The unique identifier that defines the printer in the system that uses the current print station. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the printer selected. |- | '''Active''' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the printer is active. |- | '''User''' | The user that is assigned to the specified printer ID. When a specific user is selected, only said user will have access to the printer and label model for printing. If no user is selected and the field is left blank, it indicates that anyone has access to the specified printer and printing can be done without restrictions. |- | '''Workgroup''' | Workgroup can be assigned printers such that a specific workgroup will be allowed to print labels to the specified printer. Workgroup works with the Company Tree ([~/?ScreenId=EP204061|EP204061]) form. |- | '''Owner''' | An owner can be assigned to a printer. Similar to the user, only the specified owner will be allowed to print a label to the printer. |- | '''Printer ID''' | The printer ID of the printer used for printing. Whenever print job is requested, the label will be sent the the specified printer. The list of printers to select from is configured in the [cc1f569a-e509-4277-86f0-713e588bab2e|Label Printers] ([~/?ScreenId=AL203000|AL203000]) form. |- | '''Last Modified By''' | The user name of the person who last modified the label printer. |- | '''Last Modified On''' | The date when the record was modified most recently. {br} |}[anchor|#11] ==Related Articles== *[cc1f569a-e509-4277-86f0-713e588bab2e|Label Printers]

Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AL206000|AL206000])[anchor|#_da80ec49-7fcd-453f-9347-8fea2cd39f32]{br}
On this form, you can create, view, and edit barcode contents. Barcode contents are the contents associated to the identifiers of the barcode standard. With every identifier, there can be different forms of content contained within it, which is then possibly followed by a closing (or separating) special character. {br}
{TOC}
==Form Toolbar== [anchor|#_98898224-20bf-49fd-a9f1-0289e7377fe4] The form toolbar includes standard and form-specific buttons and commands. For the list of standard buttons, see [dfac4724-edbc-468e-9569-877c174ac871|Form Toolbar]. The form-specific commands (which can be shown as buttons on the form toolbar, as commands on the More menu, or in both places) are listed in the following table in alphabetical order. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Command !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Render''' | Renders a barcode according to the elements placed in the content The rendered barcode displays the value inputted in the sample value column of the identifier from the Elements Tab. |- | '''Change ID''' | Gives you the ability to change the ID of the currently selected content. |}[anchor|#1] ==Summary Area== In this area, you can select an existing barcode content by its unique identifier or specify summary information about new barcode content. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Element !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Content ID''' | The unique identifier for the barcode content. |- | '''Active''' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the content is active in the system. |- | '''Export''' | A check box that includes (if selected) the content to the export all file. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the barcode content entered. |- | '''Screen ID''' | The screen that the content is mapped to. |- | '''Graph Type''' | The graph that is associated with the chosen screen that the content is mapped to. |- | '''Standard'' | The standard that is associated to the content defined. Every content must be linked to a standard in order to define/populate the identifiers. |- | '''Rendering Barcode ID''' | Selector allows you to choose which barcode you would like to render your content in. |- | '''Format''' | Selector allows you to choose the format of the rendered content. |- | '''Render Message''' | The messages or warnings displayed in case of a rendering issue. |}[anchor|#2] ==Elements== The '''Used by Models''' tab contains the list of label models that use the current rule. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Active'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the identifier is active in the system |- | '''Identifier''' | The identifier to be defined. |- | '''HRI Char.''' | |- | '''Enable when''' | The rule that indicates when the expression line for the element should be displayed on the label. This allows you to set lines or fields on the label that are specific to a particular condition while still being able to maintain the overall appearance of the label. The set of rules to select from are set in the [c8dd0464-39d9-42e3-a05e-7ef5715c266a|Label Rules] ([~/?ScreenId=AL203500|AL203500]) form. |- | '''Not'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the contrary of the rule applied will be in effect. |- | '''Short Name''' | The name of the identifier. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the identifier selected. |- | '''Expr. Type''' | The type of the following expression definition. Each type make a different call or reference to different functions and contents. The following types are available: *''Fixed'': The fixed type refers to any expression that is static. For instance, a string or sample value. These fields will always keep their same value. *''Screen'': The screen type refers to dynamic fields that pull their data from the respective screen that the model is mapped to. These fields will change depending on the data found in your system. *''Function'': The function type refers to the use of ZPL functions to implement the expression. *''Content'': The content type refers to the mapping of Content to the expression. Typically this is used when there is a 2D barcode that contains different identifiers. *''Image'': The image type refers to the use of an image on the label. By setting the image type, you are essentially calling the include function to bring in your image. *''Snippet'': The snippet type refers to a call of a snippet to be placed on the label. *''Same'': The same type means that the expression has the same type as the previous row (previous expression). |- | '''Expression''' | The variable that is pulled from the view written as an expression. From the tree selector, you can select which variable you want to assign to the identifier. |- | '''Sample Type''' | The type of the following sample expression definition. Each type make a different call or reference to different functions and contents. The following types are available: *''Fixed'': The fixed type refers to any expression that is static. For instance, a string or sample value. These fields will always keep their same value. *''Screen'': The screen type refers to dynamic fields that pull their data from the respective screen that the model is mapped to. These fields will change depending on the data found in your system. *''Function'': The function type refers to the use of ZPL functions to implement the expression. *''Content'': The content type refers to the mapping of Content to the expression. Typically this is used when there is a 2D barcode that contains different identifiers. *''Image'': The image type refers to the use of an image on the label. By setting the image type, you are essentially calling the include function to bring in your image. *''Snippet'': The snippet type refers to a call of a snippet to be placed on the label. *''Same'': The same type means that the expression has the same type as the previous row (previous expression). |- | '''Sample Value''' | The sample value used for the identifier. |- | '''Do Substitute''' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that a substitution is to be used. |- | '''Substitution''' | The substitution that is going to be applied to your expression. Substitutions refer to functions that are used as a means to manipulate the data whether that is to format, sort, calculate, etc. Substitutions are configured in the [e3990d02-4890-48b3-8d01-511bad4776cd|Substitutions] form. |- | '''Barcode Char.''' | Special characters are the first 32 characters of the ASCII table which are unprintable control codes. They are used to control peripherals such as printers. In the context for standards, these special characters would be used as separators between identifiers. |- | '''Last Modified By''' | The user name of the person who last modified the identifier row. |- | '''Last Modified On''' | The date when the record was modified most recently. |}[anchor|#11] ==Used By Models Tab== The '''Used by Models''' tab contains the list of label models that use the current content. The system automatically enters the models in the list as they are assigned the rule from the [17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] form. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Model ID''' | The unique identifier that defines the label model in the system that uses the current content. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the label model selected. |- | '''Code''' | The code identifier of the line expression that uses the current content. |- | '''Active''' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the model is active in the system |- | '''Last Modified By''' | The user name of the person who last modified the content. |- | '''Last Modified On''' | The date when the record was modified most recently. {br} |}[anchor|#12] ==Related Articles== *[911cc53f-4a4a-4910-bb1a-8951cb0bb504|Model Barcode] *[c9c59c19-837e-4d25-bb6f-faaf312fd8a3|Barcode Standards] *[https://www.gs1.org/standards/barcodes/application-identifiers|GS1 Application Identifiers] *[https://www.utm.edu/staff/lholder/csci201/ascii_table.pdf|ASCII Table]

Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AL304000|AL304000])[anchor|#_da80ec49-7fcd-453f-9347-8fea2cd39f32]{br}
On this form, you can create, view, and edit justification. Justification is a form of text manipulation. Defined between a range/area, the text on a label can be justified to the left, right, center or occupy the full space in the area. {br}{TOC}
==Form Toolbar== [anchor|#_dde93fc1-1961-4747-9712-d102cbed1af1] The form toolbar includes standard and form-specific buttons and commands. For the list of standard buttons, see [dfac4724-edbc-468e-9569-877c174ac871|Form Toolbar]. The form-specific commands are listed in the following table. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Button !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Extract From Models''' | An action button that will create, or update a data source element coming from a label model. |}[anchor|#1]
==Summary Area== In this area, you can select an existing justifications by its unique identifier or specify summary information about a new category. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Element !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Justification ID''' | The unique identifier of the justification. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the justification. |- | '''Justification''' | The type of the following justification. Each justification manipulates the text differently. The following justifications are available: *''Center'': The text will align itself at the center of the defined range. *''Full'': The text will occupy the full space of the defined range. *''Left'': The text will align itself to the left of the defined range *''Right'': The text will align itself to the right of the defined range. |- | '''Active'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the justfication is active in the system |- | '''Export''' | A check box that includes (if selected) the justification to the export all file. |- | '''From X''' | The x-position of the justification range. The beginning of the range for the justification. The x-axis is the horizontal axis of the label. |- | '''To X''' | The end x-position of the justification range. A justification will be made in relation to the range defined by From. X to X. The x-axis is the horizontal axis of the label. |- | '''Max Lines''' | The number of lines affected by the justification. |- | '''Size Unit''' | The unit of measure dictating the length of the justfication. The following options are available: *''inch'': The unit of measure that corresponds to an inch. *''cm'': The unit of measure that corresponds to a centimeter. *''mm'': The unit of measure that corresponds to a millimeter. *''dot'': The unit of measure that corresponds to a printer dots. |- | '''Space b/w Lines (+/-)''' | The space between the lines. |- | '''Hanging Indent''' | Indent the text further away from the justification |}[anchor|#2] ==Used By Models Tab== The '''Used By Models''' tab contains the list of label models that implement the current justification. The system automatically lists the models as they are assigned to the category from the [17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] form. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Model ID''' | The unique identifier that defines the label model in the system that uses the current category. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the label model selected. |- | '''Code''' | The expression code that the data element is mapped to |- | '''Active'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the label model is active in the system |- | '''Last Modified By''' | The user name of the person who last modified the category assignment of label. |- | '''Last Modified On''' | The date when the record was modified most recently. |}[anchor|#11]
==Related Articles== * [17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models]

Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AL503000|AL503000])[anchor|#_45addb01-b3ea-4ac1-ac1a-7bd345cb7ffd]
{br}
You use this form to reprint or delete label records that were printed. You can use the numerous filters to locate the specific label you want to reprint or delete. Once the specific label is found, reprinting is done from the View Print Log * ([~/?ScreenId=AL203010|AL203010]) screen.
{TOC}
==Form Toolbar== [anchor|#_dde93fc1-1961-4747-9712-d102cbed1af1] The form toolbar includes standard and form-specific buttons and commands. For the list of standard buttons, see [dfac4724-edbc-468e-9569-877c174ac871|Form Toolbar]. The form-specific commands are listed in the following table. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Button !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Process''' | Will process the selected label record depending on the action selected: print or delete. |- | '''Process All''' | Will process all the label records depending on the action selected: print or delete. |}[anchor|#1] ==Selection Area== In the Selection area, you can select the label records to be listed (and processed, if needed) by account, model, screen, printer assigned, print station, format, label key and/or filename. Also, you can select the creation date for the label to be generated. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Element !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Action''' | A drop down box to select which action will occur during the processing of the selected label record when the Process action button is clicked. |- | '''Start Date''' | The beginning date range for which the label was printed. |- | '''End Date''' | The end date range for which the label was printed. |- | '''Content Type''' | The file type in which the label model is processed. Could be a printer programming language or a file type like pdf, png, gif, json. *''Datamax'': Datamax Programming Language, also known as DPL, is Datamax Barcode printer's control language. Datamax is a subsidiary of Honeywell. *''Eltron'': Eltron Programming Language, also known as EPL, is Eltron's printer control language. *''Intermec'': Intermec Printer Language, also known as IPL, is the printer control language used with Intermec printers. *''Sato'': SATO Barcode Printer Language, also known as SBPL, is the printer control language that is used to communicate from the PC to the printer to define the label format and label printing program as well as setting of the printer operational mode. *''Zebra'': Zebra Programming Language, also known as ZPL, is Zebra Technologies' printer control language used for making their labels and label models. |- | '''B. Account''' | In Acumatica ERP, a business account represents a legal entity (a company or a person) that your organization deals with or intends to sell products and services to. |- | '''User ID''' | Acumatica Users that have access to the site that have printed a label. |- | '''Owner''' | The name of the individual linked to the user ID. |- | '''Model ID''' | The label model that was printed. |- | '''Screen ID''' | The screen from which the label model is mapped to and printed from. |- | '''Printer ID''' | The printer from which the label model was printed from. |- | '''New Printer ID''' | A selector to choose which printer the reprint of the label will occur. |- | '''Print Station ID''' | The print station from which the label model was printed from. |- | '''Format ID''' | The format of the label model. |- | '''Label Key''' | A text box to enter the unique identifying key for the label model for a more specific filtering. |- | '''Filename''' | A text box to enter the name of the printed label file for a more specific filtering. |} ==Labels Tab== The '''Labels''' tab contains the list of label records found based on the filters applied in the selection area. Records in the list can be selected for processing. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Toolbar=== [anchor|#_90532f1d-22ca-490d-9fff-e83f1ce3e5fe] The table toolbar includes standard buttons and buttons that are specific to this table. For the list of standard buttons, see [53fbbe04-a46c-4975-93c4-1d342170e472|Table Toolbar]. The table-specific buttons are listed below. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Button !width="79%" ! Description |- | '''Email Photo Logs''' | Action button to send an email from your user to a recipient with the label file as an attachment. |- | '''Export Photo Logs''' | Action button to export the label file in a zip file. |}
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Selected''' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the label record is chosen for processing. |- | '''Record ID''' | The unique identifier of the printed label record. |- | '''Created On''' | The date and time where the label was created and printed. |- | '''B. Account''' | The business account that the label was printed for. |- | '''Model'' | The label model of the printed label. |- | '''Filename''' | The file name of the printed label |- | '''Label Key''' | The unique key that identifies the label record. |- | '''Image'' | The image of the printed label. |- | '''Screen''' | The screen from which the label was printed. |- | '''Print Station''' | The print station from which the label was printed. |- | '''Printer''' | The printer that printed the label. |- | '''Format''' | The format size of the label. |- | '''Format''' | The format of the paper stock on the printer. |- | '''User''' | The user that printed the label. |- | '''Owner''' | The unique identifier of the owner account that printed the label. |- | '''Content Type''' | The programming language that the label was written in. |- | '''Nb. of Labels''' | The number of labels that were printed. |} [anchor|#3] ==Related Articles== *[4c04829e-b227-499e-afc7-f14a958190d3|View Print Log] ([~/?ScreenId=AL203010|AL203010]) *[17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] ([~/?ScreenId=AL201000|AL201000])

Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AL502000|AL502000]){br}
On this form, you can select the label file, specify criteria for selecting label model to be considered for deletion, and delete all of the filtered label files or only selected ones.
==Selection Area== In this area, you can define the criteria for the label files to be displayed in the table, as well as the action to be applied if you click '''Delete''' or '''Delete All'''.[anchor|#table_g2j_4ms_2bb] {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Element !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Screen ID''' | The screen that the label files is attached to. |- | '''End Date''' | The end date of the date range for when the label files we created. You can leave the box blank to view all label files. |}[anchor|#2] ==Table== This table contains the list of print jobs of label model that match any criteria specified in the Selection area. You can select print jobs for processing by using the check boxes in the select column. [anchor|#table_vfj_4ms_2bb] {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Select''' | A check box that you select to include the label file in processing when you click Delete. |- | '''File''' | The GUID of the label file. |- | '''Name''' | The name of the label file. |- | '''Graph Type''' | The graph that is associated with the chosen label file. |- | '''Entity Type''' | The portion of the screen which the label file is mapped to. |- | '''Comment''' | A comment that describes the label file. The comments can vary and can describe the user and date of the label rendering, or the name of the label. |- | '''Creation Time''' | The date and time when the label file was created. |}

Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AL202500|AL202500])[anchor|#_da80ec49-7fcd-453f-9347-8fea2cd39f32]{br}
On this form, you can create, view, and edit colors that you want to place on labels. Colors can be used on [17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] ([~/?ScreenId=AL201000|AL201000]) to allow your label to enhance communication and differentiate. In other words, you can use colors to your labels to convey a particular meaning to warehouse workers or distributors. For instance, red could signify warning or hazardous products, green could be eco-friendly, etc. Colors can also allow your labels to stand out from the standard black and white label. {br}
{TOC}
==Summary Area== In this area, you can select an existing colors by its unique identifier or specify summary information about a new model rule. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Element !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Color ID''' | The unique identifier for the color. |- | '''Active'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the color is active in the system |- | '''Export'' | A check box that includes (if selected) the color to the export all file. |- | '''Is Composite'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the color can belong to a set of rules where depending on the condition fulfilled, a different color will appear on the label. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the color entered. |- | '''Primary Color''' | An RGB color picker to select the desired color. |- | '''Alpha''' | The Alpha channel specifies the opacity for a color. The Alpha Value can be measured as a Real Value, a Percentage, or an Integer: The full transparency is defined as 0.0 ; 0% or 0, visualized in the alpha channel image as pure black. The full opacity is defined as 1.0, 100%, or 255, visualized in the alpha channel image as pure white. |- | '''Red'' | The red code value from the RGB color picker. |- | '''Green''' | The green code value from the RGB color picker. |- | '''Blue''' | The blue code value from the RGB color picker. |}[anchor|#2]
==Used By Expressions Tab== The '''Used by Expressions''' tab contains the list of label expressions that use the current rule. The system automatically enters the expressions in the list as they are assigned the color from the [17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] form. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Model ID''' | The unique identifier that defines the label model in the system that uses the current color. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the label model selected. |- | '''Code''' | The code identifier of the line expression that uses the current color. |- | '''Last Modified By''' | The user name of the person who last modified the user, printer ID, or duplicate in toolbar checkbox. |- | '''Last Modified On''' | The date when the record was modified most recently. {br} |}[anchor|#11]
==Used By Rules Tab== The '''Used by Rules''' tab contains the list of rules that use the current color. The system automatically enters the rules in the list as they are assigned the color from the [c8dd0464-39d9-42e3-a05e-7ef5715c266a|Rules] form. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Color ID''' | The unique identifier that defines the color in the system that the model rule uses. |- | '''Rule ID''' | The unique identifier that defines the rule in the system that the color is mapped to. |- | '''Last Modified By''' | The user name of the person who last modified the user, printer ID, or duplicate in toolbar checkbox. |- | '''Last Modified On''' | The date when the record was modified most recently. {br} |}[anchor|#11] ==Rule Detail Tab== The '''Rule Detail''' tab allows you to assign colors to different rules. Depending on a particular condition, a color will be printed on the label. This tab appears only if the ''Is Composite'' check box is enabled in the summary area of this form. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Business Account''' | The unique identifier for the Business Account that the rule can be tied to. |- | '''Active'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the rule is active in the system |- | '''Use When'' | The unique identifier of the model rule that the color will fill depending on the condition. |- | '''Reverse'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the opposite of the rule must apply to the current composite rule. |- | '''Child Color''' | The unique identifier for the color that the composite rule follows. |}[anchor|#11] ==Related Articles== *[17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] *[c8dd0464-39d9-42e3-a05e-7ef5715c266a|Rules]

Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AL303500|AL303500])[anchor|#_da80ec49-7fcd-453f-9347-8fea2cd39f32]{br}
On this form, you can create, view, and edit data element. Data Elements are the expressions that allows the label to pull data from the Acumatica screen or print hardcoded values onto the label. Instead of writing out the label expressions, data elements breaks down the expression into different components. Data elements are also reusable. Once it is defined, the element can be reused on any label which simplifies the label mapping process. {br}{TOC}
==Summary Area== In this area, you can select an existing data elements by its unique identifier or specify summary information about a new category. {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Element !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Data Element''' | The unique identifier of the data element. |- | '''Source ID''' | The source of the data element. A source could be an Acumatica screen or could be a general source that does not involve pulling data from a screen, such as hardcoded values. Sources are configured in the [3cd04c1d-167b-41e2-9046-3b571fd39c88|Data Source] form. |- | '''Expr. Type''' | The type of the following expression definition. Each type make a different call or reference to different functions and contents. The following types are available: *''Hardcoded'': The fixed type refers to any expression that is static. For instance, a string or sample value. These fields will always keep their same value. *''Screen'': The screen type refers to dynamic fields that pull their data from the respective screen that the model is mapped to. These fields will change depending on the data found in your system. *''Function'': The function type refers to the use of ZPL functions to implement the expression. *''Content'': The content type refers to the mapping of Content to the expression. Typically this is used when there is a 2D barcode that contains different identifiers. *''Image'': The image type refers to the use of an image on the label. By setting the image type, you are essentially calling the include function to bring in your image. *''Snippet'': The snippet type refers to a call of a snippet to be placed on the label. |- | '''Active'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the data element is active in the system |- | '''Export''' | A check box that includes (if selected) the data element to the export all file. |- | '''Based On''' | The name of the view that the screen expression is based on. |- | '''Expression''' | The expression that pulls the data value from the screen or the hardcoded value. |- | '''Default Value''' | The default value given to the expression if no dat is found or pulled from the database. |- | '''Do Substitute''' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that a substitution is to be used. |- | '''Substitution''' | The substitution that is going to be applied to your expression. Substitutions refer to functions that are used as a means to manipulate the data whether that is to format, sort, calculate, etc. Substitutions are configured in the [e3990d02-4890-48b3-8d01-511bad4776cd|Substitutions] form. |- | '''Barcode ID''' | The barcode that the expression or sample value will take form in. Barcodes are configured in the [911cc53f-4a4a-4910-bb1a-8951cb0bb504|Barcodes] form. |- | '''Category''' | The category attributed to the defined expression. |- | '''Sample Type''' | The type of the following sample expression definition. Each type make a different call or reference to different functions and contents. The following types are available: *''Fixed'': The fixed type refers to any expression that is static. For instance, a string or sample value. These fields will always keep their same value. *''Screen'': The screen type refers to dynamic fields that pull their data from the respective screen that the model is mapped to. These fields will change depending on the data found in your system. *''Function'': The function type refers to the use of ZPL functions to implement the expression. *''Content'': The content type refers to the mapping of Content to the expression. Typically this is used when there is a 2D barcode that contains different identifiers. *''Image'': The image type refers to the use of an image on the label. By setting the image type, you are essentially calling the include function to bring in your image. *''Snippet'': The snippet type refers to a call of a snippet to be placed on the label. *''Same'': The same type means that the expression has the same type as the previous row (previous expression). |- | '''Sample Based On''' | The information that the sample is based on. |- | '''Sample Value''' | The value used in the rendering process of the label. Sample values are independent of the values used for printing. |}[anchor|#2] ==Used By Models Tab== The '''Used By Models''' tab contains the list of label models that implement the current data element. The system automatically lists the models as they are assigned to the category from the [17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] form. [anchor|#table_sss_gpd_cj]
===Table Columns === {| class="checklist" | width="100%" |- !width="20%" ! Column !width="80%" ! Description |- | '''Model ID''' | The unique identifier that defines the label model in the system that uses the current category. |- | '''Description''' | A brief description of the label model selected. |- | '''Code''' | The expression code that the data element is mapped to |- | '''Active'' | A check box that indicates (if selected) that the data element is active in the system |- | '''Last Modified By''' | The user name of the person who last modified the category assignment of label. |- | '''Last Modified On''' | The date when the record was modified most recently. |}[anchor|#11]
==Related Articles== * [17d7fda8-adf8-4205-8329-5a35d0dfec49|Label Models] * [3cd04c1d-167b-41e2-9046-3b571fd39c88|Data Source]

